        "question_text": "<p>Which heat treatment process involves heating steel to a temperature above its critical range and then cooling it <i>slowly</i> in a furnace?</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>Annealing involves heating steel above its critical temperature and then cooling it slowly in a furnace to relieve internal stresses, improve machinability, and soften the metal. Quenching involves rapid cooling, tempering involves reheating after quenching, and normalizing involves air cooling.</p>",
